Yeah. And because the early AI-nimes are already fun, there’s a reason to keep making them. The scene can have a weird cut, a ridiculous line, and still make you want to know what happens next. That gives the person making it something concrete to practice on the next episode.

Take Previously, in a Different Life. The early version has the wife gasp, “You have his memories!” Thunder cracks. Cut to credits. I’d watch that. A few episodes later, you’ve learned to let the scene breathe. She hands him a peach. He cuts it into quarters and gives her the smallest one.

“Why’d you give me that piece?”

“You always save the biggest for last.”

She puts it down. She’s never told him that.

Same cheesy premise. Now you can feel why it hurts. And you might still keep the thunder.